  "plan": {
    "goal": "Flow-limited (high-extraction) propranolol clearance study in a perfused liver-on-chip, targeting E=0.8 so clearance reflects perfusion rather than intrinsic enzyme capacity.",
    "rationale": "Propranolol is a high-extraction (flow-limited) drug (E>0.7, Rowland & Tozer). We target E=0.8 (inlet 10 uM, outlet 2 uM) so that clearance Cl=E*Q reflects perfusion rate, not CYP capacity. At 1 uL/min perfusion, Cl=0.8 uL/min. HepG2 (liver, BSL-1) is used as a metabolically active hepatocyte model; seeded at 75,000 cells/cm2 (within the 50,000-100,000 range) on a 0.08 cm2 channel floor (~6,000 cells). A 400x100 um x 20 mm PDMS channel gives laminar flow (Re~0.07) and a residence time of ~48 s at 1 uL/min. System volume 200 uL gives t1/2 ~2.9 h. A cell-free control isolates cell-mediated clearance from PDMS/tubing binding. Sample size 4/group detects an E difference of 0.2 (SD 0.1) at 80% power.",
