    "caveats": [
      "At the specified 1 uL/min flow, wall shear is ~0.025 Pa, below the HepG2 physiological range (0.05-0.15 Pa); if shear fidelity matters, run at ~4 uL/min for 0.1 Pa and scale the clearance readout accordingly.",
      "Propranolol is a high-extraction drug; verify the measured E stays >0.7 to confirm the flow-limited regime (if E drops below ~0.3, the model is capacity-limited and the flow-limited interpretation is invalid).",
      "Include a cell-free (no-cell) chip control to subtract PDMS/tubing binding from the measured clearance.",
      "Confirm the LC-MS/MS assay can resolve the ~0.12 ug/h cleared mass at 10 uM inlet.",
      "HepG2 is an immortalized line, not primary human hepatocytes; intrinsic CYP activity differs from PHH - validate with a known high-extraction probe if quantitative PK is the goal.",
      "Verify the 1 uL/min flow is stable and the pump can hold it; pressure drop is only ~10 Pa so backpressure is not a concern."
    ]
